.TH MJPEGMOUNT 1 "October 2026" "mjpegsuite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mjpegmount \- mount an mjpegstore set as seekable .mkv files (FUSE)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mjpegmount
[\-f] [\-d] [\-o OPTION,...] SETDIR MOUNTPOINT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mounts an mjpegstore set read\-only. Every clip in SETDIR (a subdirectory of JPEG pictures made by mjpegstore \-i) appears as CLIP.mkv: the same bytes mjpegstore \-s writes (one V_MJPEG track in Matroska), except for the writing\-application name in the header, but as a seekable file, so a player, encoder or editor can open it without anything being exported first.
.PP
Every size in the file follows from the sizes of the picture files, so a read at any offset maps onto a few header bytes and the picture files behind them. Nothing is decoded, re\-encoded or scanned, and only the pictures a read touches are opened. The picture files can live anywhere, on a plain disk or on another mount.
.PP
SETDIR may also be a single clip directory (specs.txt in its parent). A valid specs.txt is required; it supplies the frame rate and size and cannot be generated on a read\-only mount. Progressive sets only. Unmount with fusermount3 \-u MOUNTPOINT. Needs libfuse3.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Stay in the foreground; errors are printed to the terminal.
.TP
.B \-d
Foreground, plus libfuse debug output.
.TP
.B \-o OPT,...
Mount options passed to libfuse, such as allow_other.
